### Step 4: Exception Handling Ke 5 Main Keywords

Java me Exception Handling in 5 keywords par chalti hai:

1. `try`: Risk wala code likhne ke liye.
2. `catch`: Exception ko pakadne (handle karne) ke liye.
3. `finally`: Ye block hamesha chalega, chahe error aaye ya na aaye (e.g., file close karna, database disconnect karna).
4. `throw`: Apni marzi se koi custom exception throw (raise) karne ke liye.
5. `throws`: Function ke aage declare karne ke liye ki ye function exception de sakta hai.

---

### Step 5: `finally`, `throw`, aur `throws` Ka Code Example

#### 1. `finally` Block Example

```java
try {
    int data = 25 / 5;
    System.out.println("Data: " + data);
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println(e);
} finally {
    // Ye line HAR HALAT ME chalegi
    System.out.println("Finally block: Main hamesha chalta hu!");
}

```

#### 2. `throw` Keyword Example (Custom Validation)

```java
public class AgeChecker {
    public static void checkAge(int age) {
        if (age < 18) {
            // Manual error throw kar rahe hain
            throw new ArithmeticException("Voting ke liye age 18+ honi chahiye!");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Aap vote de sakte hain!");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            checkAge(15);
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Exception pakdi gayi: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}

```

